WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.390
Smart people think nobody else can do their
work better than them.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:10.700
Nobody So they have to control everything
they're doing.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.990
Millionaires eventually figure out that if
you want to scale and build a very big business

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:19.340
and become a millionaire one day, you have
to learn that you can't do it all by yourself,

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.950
and you need a lot of help.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.070
So they go from being smart to being wise.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.480
And to become wise, you learn how to delegate
and leverage.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.439
So today, we're going to talk about a word
that most control freaks cannot stand.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:33.439
And it's called delegation.

00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:38.500
And I know it may be a curse word to you and
I know it's not the most exciting topic you

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.050
may want to watch, but I promise you by the
time we're done, you're going to fall in love

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.050
with delegation.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.670
Because I'm going to talk about in this video
11 laws of delegation, and I'm going to talk

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.780
about what things you cannot delegate.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.420
So maybe one day, you can get out of your
own way and build a business and enjoy the

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.420
fruits of your labor.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.030
Okay, so law #1 is to delegate up.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.340
You've got to learn how to delegate up.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.700
So what does delegate up mean?

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.469
When we first started the YouTube channel,
I can't edit, so I delegate up.

00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:08.499
We bring Paul.

00:01:08.499 --> 00:01:10.850
That's delegate up.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.420
When it came out to compliance, I'm not the
best in compliance, we delegate up.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:15.990
We went and got somebody.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.060
When it comes down to all these different
projects we're working on, with websites,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.119
these apps that cost a million dollars we're
designing right now, we can't do it, so we

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:29.189
have engineers who are experts at code, from
all over the world that we delegated up to,

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:33.741
and they're producing products that's insane
of a product they're producing for us, because

00:01:33.741 --> 00:01:35.409
we learned how to delegate up.

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:39.119
The better you are at delegating up, the better
products you produce, the better systems you

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:41.090
create, the better company you create.

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:42.090
Law #2.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.619
Number two is, while you are delegating up,
think about it this way.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:52.381
So this certain task, put hours to it, will
take eight hours if you do it, 12 hours if

00:01:52.381 --> 00:01:53.399
somebody else does it.

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:55.609
So let's go based on 12 hours.

00:01:55.609 --> 00:02:01.899
If this task is going to take 12 hours to
do it, and it costs you $250, which is $25

00:02:01.899 --> 00:02:07.310
bucks an hour to get this other person to
do it, but you can do it in eight hours.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.430
Eight hours, that's $30 per hour to you.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.860
Are you worth more than $30 an hour?

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.810
This other person can do it.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:20.280
With those 12 hours that you have, what can
you do to use your 12 hours effectively to

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.290
help grow the company?

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.379
Because if you grow the company, this person
has more of a steady job.

00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:28.319
And you can pay him more money, because your
brain can be in a place to say what can I

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:33.980
do to expand the company, and work on my business
so I can grow it even to a whole different

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:34.980
level.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.230
You see, there's a big difference in thinking
when you learn how to delegate up and you

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:42.090
learn how to take this task that takes 12
hours, put it effectively in the different

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.540
area of your business to grow it.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.829
Law #3: Just because you're best at it does
mean you need to do it.

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:50.650
Just because you're best at it doesn't mean
you need to do it.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.269
A lot of times you're going to be the best
at it.

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:54.030
That doesn't mean you need to do it.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:59.380
I can be very, very effective in doing case
management work on the complete other side

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.659
of the building with our company.

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:02.260
I'd be phenomenal at it.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.630
But I'm not going to do it.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.909
The company needs me in a complete different
position than they need me sitting there doing

00:03:06.909 --> 00:03:07.909
case management.

00:03:07.909 --> 00:03:11.530
I am more effective for the company doing
the work that I'm doing right now, because

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.920
I don't need to do that.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.930
That's called just because I can do it better
than them doesn't mean I need to be doing

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:16.930
it.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:20.470
Law #4, force yourself NOT to do it.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.470
Sometimes it's like an addict.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.500
You know it's like an addict.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.740
They can't let go of something they're addicted
to.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:30.069
You have no idea how much control freaks are
just addicted to doing everything themselves.

00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:31.069
No, no, no.

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:32.219
I'm going to do it myself.

00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:34.090
And they fire people galore.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.319
You know how I know that?

00:03:35.319 --> 00:03:40.730
I fired 27 assistants in my first two years
of my career 13 years ago.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.730
You know why?

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.370
Because I didn't think any one of my assistants
could do it as good as me.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.370
None of them.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.370
I could do better than everybody.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.370
And I was right.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.290
But I was not growing at the pace I wanted
to grow.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.530
The moment I delegated, I put four or five
assistants around me.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.739
We just went phoom!

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:58.340
We exploded, because I was finally using my
time in proper areas to grow the business

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.599
that effectively grew everyone else's business.

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:03.549
And all those people that were assistants
making a couple grand a year, right now they're

00:04:03.549 --> 00:04:04.549
making a lot more money.

00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:08.670
So I was beneficial to everybody if I made
a decision to force myself to not have to

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:09.670
do all the work.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.370
Now, let's go to the next one.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.130
If you're going to delegate, there's one area
you're going to be judged on as a person that's

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.130
going to delegate.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.440
And here's what it is.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:27.420
You will be judged on how you duplicate a
certain person that you delegate a task to

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:28.760
that you no longer want to do.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:34.530
For instance, I want to teach this person
how to do front desk answering the phones.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.630
It will take me 18 hours to teach Bob how
to answer the phones.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.250
So I'm going to role play with Bob.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.910
I need you to do this, do this, do this, and
I'm going to role play, role play, role play.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:43.910
. . you got it.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:44.910
. . Pretty easy?

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:45.910
Okay, great.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:46.910
So I'm just giving the numbers.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:50.030
Let's just say it takes seven hours.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.680
So Bob is now doing the front desk.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.770
He now has a script.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.000
We've role played a million times.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.190
He now knows how to do it.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.680
I delegate that.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.680
Negotiation.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:01.480
Anybody that works here around me, we're going
to work very hard on you being a very good

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:06.540
negotiator and learning at what point not
to push, at what point to understand that

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.110
it's time for us to push.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.910
At some point to realize this partner's abusing
us.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.640
At what point to cut a vendor and say, "we
are no longer doing business with this vendor."

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.640
Why?

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.250
If you work closely with me, you're going
to become a better negotiator.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.130
So there will be many time we say, I want
you to listen to this negotiation call.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.080
Stand right here, and listen for the 30 minutes.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.660
And they stand right here and they listen
to me, and I go through it..

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.840
Boom, boom, boom.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:33.080
I'm duplicating negotiators that may take
a year for me to do, but a year later, I'm

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:36.940
going to say, you handle this, because I duplicated
a negotiator.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:41.140
I duplicated a negotiator that I can delegate
that task to.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:45.870
Which, by the way, that person's value also
goes higher.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:49.370
When you teach somebody else to also learn
certain skills, their value goes higher, because

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:53.130
you injected your belief, your talent, your
skill into that person.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:55.180
Their value goes higher, the company's value
goes higher.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.860
This is a smart thing to do, if you learn
how to duplicate other people that are doing

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.310
the tasks that you're doing.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.410
Next, match up accordingly.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:07.840
So you cannot match up somebody to do front
desk if they're not very good on front desk,

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.310
and they just don't like people.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:10.310
You can't match up.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.310
That's not proper delegation.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:13.800
That's not smart delegation.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.460
You can't match up somebody to do business
dev when they have a short temper.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.770
Hey, I need you to go visit all my customers
and build a relationship with them.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:21.770
Okay, great.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:22.770
They go out there and they piss everybody
off.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:23.960
They come back, why?

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.480
They had me wait 20 minutes!

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.560
It's your customers, man, you've got to wait.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:29.090
What are you doing?

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.180
We just lost that account.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.150
I don't care what it is, they made me wait!

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:33.320
That's a bad biz dev person.

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:37.830
You've got to match up accordingly, so you
can't match up just anybody to delegate any

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.830
work.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.560
You need to know, is this the perfect position
for them.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.850
Or are you asking a fish to climb a tree?

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:45.850
What are you doing with them?

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:47.080
A fish knows how to swim.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.410
That's it.

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:51.160
You don't ask a fish to climb a tree like
Einstein said, many years ago.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.020
If you do, you're going to make them feel
stupid, and they're not stupid.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.360
What is their strength?

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:59.290
Delegate it properly in the department they're
going to be able to max themselves out.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:02.710
#7 Inspect until you trust.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:03.710
Very simple.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:07.360
You can replace the word inspect as micromanage
until you trust.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.820
So I want you to take over this task from
me on a weekly basis.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.820
Great.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.060
It's three hours a week of work I'm doing.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.620
Inspect, inspect, inspect, inspect, inspect.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.620
You got it.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.620
You're on your own.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:17.620
Trust.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.040
Law #8: Be very clear on what you're expecting.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:24.620
So if I'm delegating xyz to Bobby, I got to
be clear on what I'm expecting Bobby to do.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.960
Bobby, I expect you to do boom, boom, boom.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.400
Many times we're not clear with the direction
we're giving them.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.960
They're frustrated because they don't know
how to make you happy or please you.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:34.960
There's friction.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.970
The friction is on your end, giving proper
clear expectation to the other person that

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.440
you're delegating the certain responsibility
to.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.110
This has got to be clear.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:46.440
Then they've got to come back and you've got
to ask, "Do I make myself clear?

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.480
Does this make sense to you?

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.480
Do you have any questions?"

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.480
No, I got it.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.480
Perfect.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.460
Email, document, go ahead, move on, and then
you hold them accountable.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.550
You follow up with it.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:58.420
#9, stop doing $10 an hour jobs.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.420
Okay?

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.420
Stop going $10 an hour jobs yourself.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.810
And let me explain to you what I mean by stop
doing $10 an hour jobs.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:08.150
I've said this in a few other videos before
in the past, that I loved ironing and I loved

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.150
shining my shoes.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.960
And at one point, even though I couldn't afford
it, I stopped doing both, because I had to

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.960
increase my own value.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.740
Now, sometimes when people say that, they
say, "Well, Pat, are you saying that person's

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:19.740
worth $10 an hour?"

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.420
They may.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:22.720
Yes.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.880
If a person is saying yes to a $10 an hour
job, guess what they're saying?

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.550
"That's what I'm worth."

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:33.620
If a person says yes to a $70,000 a year job,
that's what they're worth.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.360
If a person's saying yes to a $40,000 a year
job, that's what they're worth.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:39.510
Now by the way, so you may say, "I'm going
to say no to those job offers."

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:43.240
Then you're not very smart because if that's
what truly your value in the marketplace,

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:44.800
you saying no, that means you're unemployed.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.800
So what's a wise position for you to make?

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:48.800
Right?

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:53.251
So, first of all, yes, this person is willing
to choose to take this work for $10, and you

00:08:53.251 --> 00:08:55.440
shouldn't be doing it at as an entrepreneur
that wants to scale.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.900
You need to go to the wise side, not just
the smart side.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.850
Now, watch this.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:05.820
You better understand that this person is
just as important as anybody else on the team.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.580
This is a very valuable position on what you're
doing.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.260
If you delegate a responsibility to somebody
and they don't know how important it is, they're

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:14.690
not going to do the work to the best of their
abilities.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:18.360
So you've got to make that very clear with
somebody when you give them certain tasks

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.420
for them to do.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:20.870
#10: Hire project managers.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.560
I like hiring project managers.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:26.560
Right now we're working on a certain project
that's very, very big.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.480
We don't have the time to do everything ourselves.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.950
I have a project manager I hired from Australia
who is the best of the best.

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.080
He's phenomenal at what he does.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.270
He gives me reports.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.970
I know exactly what's going on.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.140
He does it, sends us emails.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.140
We get on a Skype.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.140
We get on a call.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.130
I found this guy myself personally.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:42.130
I recruited him.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:43.350
He's exceptional.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:46.210
And we're going to do business with him for
many, many, many years to come.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.740
Initially it was supposed to be a 10-hour
job that we did.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:51.520
I think we've done so many hours of work right
now, we'll be doing business for the next

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.880
ten years together.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.510
Hire project managers that allows you to do
the bigger things to grow the business.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.080
Last law here.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.080
Number 11.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.080
Be a leader.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:03.630
Be a leader.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.830
Not a doer of all.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:06.850
Let me say it again.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:09.570
Be a leader, not a doer of all.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.510
A lot of times we say things like, "He's a
doer.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:13.510
He does everything himself.

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:14.510
He's a doer.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.510
He's a doer."

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.510
Great.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:21.310
Be a doer of where you increase the value
of your abilities in the company.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:24.000
And everybody else is the highest possible.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.000
Be a doer there.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.580
Not be a doer of everything.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.580
Nope.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:28.840
Be a leader.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:32.260
Lead, and do the areas that you are very good
at.

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:33.260
Do those things.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.260
Not do it all.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:35.730
When you first start a business, you're going
to do all.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:39.520
When you first start a business, you're going
to do compliance, you're going to do operations.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:40.520
When I first.

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:44.740
. . I'm doing negotiations, customer service,
front desk, issues, complaints.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:48.230
I am doing every single thing you can be thinking
about when we first started.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:50.830
Every single thing you can be thinking about,
I'm doing it.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:51.860
